hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"193","Muhammad bin Yahya and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi al-Najood, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan bin Assal Al-Muradi, and he said: What brings you? I said: I have come to impart knowledge. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No outsider goes out of his house to seek Knowledge, unless the angels spread their wings for him, content with what he is doing.” He said: I have come to you to ask you about wiping over the socks. He said: Yes, we were in the army that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent. So He commanded us to wipe over the socks when we put them in to purify ourselves, three days when we travel, and one night when we stay, and not to take them off. Neither defecate nor urinate, and we do not take them off except in case of ritual impurity.” He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “In Morocco there is a door open for repentance that will last for seventy years and will not be closed until... “The sun rises in the west,” etc. Abu Bakr said: I mentioned to Al-Muzani the news of Abd al-Razzaq, and he said: He narrated this to our companions, for Al-Shafi’i does not have a stronger argument than This"
